  "findings": {
    "197": "The new diagnostic module has a registered bounded current-target service-input/receive/source contract. This resolves only the missing-registration dimension, not the complete module or source198.",
    "198": "Existing source passes outer relay payload directly to game-message queues and sends raw game-message bytes. It lacks the current inner tag/u64 sequence/data-control admission layer. Recover the send sequence producer, inner encoder, per-peer pending-message/replay/ACK/reset lifecycle and clock ownership before implementing this cohesive relay repair.",
    "199": "Missing wire31 outer service decoder and dispatch: tag31 plus little-endian u32 peer id maps to native variant0xb. Peer0 writes service+1e2 from active-guest flag; existing host peer writes its second flag true. Actual source rejects tag31. Recover the flag consumer, producer/reset lifecycle and delivery effect before selected repair; no stronger connected/ready meaning is assumed.",
    "200": "Missing wire32 outer service decoder and dispatch: tag32 plus little-endian u32 peer id maps to native variant0xc. Peer0 clears service+1e2; existing host peer clears its second flag. Actual source rejects tag32. Recover the flag consumer, source state owner and lifecycle before selected repair; do not equate it with ordinary peer departure."
  },
